 "notes": "Paper sets 95% C.L. upper limits on ALP-photon coupling from combined analysis of ten activity phases of Mrk 421 observed by ARGO-YBJ and Fermi-LAT. This is an astrophysical propagation bound (ALP-photon oscillation in blazar jet + Galactic magnetic fields), not a DM haloscope search, so no local DM density assumed. No numerical table provided; data points are approximate, reconstructed from text statements: limit within ~[2e-11, 6e-11] GeV^-1 for 5e-10 eV <= m_a <= 5e-7 eV, with g_agamma >~ 3e-11 GeV^-1 excluded for 5e-10 to 2e-9 eV and a region near m_a ~ 2e-7 eV below the CAST limit (6.6e-11 GeV^-1). Exact contour shape (Fig. 5/6) not extractable from text; intermediate points are interpolated estimates. Results depend on assumed jet magnetic field model (BJMF) parameters, especially B0 and r_VHE. | vector-trace candidate: fig_compare_contour_421-eps-converted-to.pdf colour (0.8, 0.0, 0.0), 73 pts (selected among 9) | selector: vector_trace over text (quality (1, 1, 1, 1, 3.5, 0, 0.85, 73))",
